                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04bf90b2-44a2-40b9-bfe9-2b8842413dca",
                                                "sense_id": "5433056d-bd18-372b-b81a-a15f9f832b60",
                                                "text": "Calm and phlegmatic, with a clear eye, Mr. Fogg seemed a perfect type of that English composure which Angelica Kauffmann has so skilfully represented on canvas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70df4bf8-bcba-4290-9514-bd82e29daef8",
                                                "sense_id": "5433056d-bd18-372b-b81a-a15f9f832b60",
                                                "text": "2013, A.O. Scott, “How It Looks to Think: Watch Her,” Rev. of Hannah Arendt, dir. by Margarethe von Trotta, New York Times 29 May 2013: C1. Print.\nTheir friendship (immortalized in a splendid volume of letters that has clearly served as one of Ms. von Trotta's sources) is a fascinating study in cultural and temperamental contrast, an impulsive and witty American paired with a steady, phlegmatic German."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
